{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457978-kyasid-alchemy","id":1457978,"title":"Kyasid alchemy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-29T08:49:45-07:00","id":1457978,"title":"Kyasid alchemy","content":"Hi darklings<br /> <br /> After rereading LotB for the Nth time, I though about discussing hypothetical devellopement of kyasid alchemy as mentioned in the book.<br /> <br /> First thing first, this is a purely V20 post, please keep V5 in it's place, which I won't mention to avoid the mod's temper.<br /> <br /> As a reminder and for those that didn't have the book, the kyasid bloodline of Marconius, a lasombra who mutated through an elixir made of weird creatures, notably the essence of the abyss and faeries, sees themselves as an alchemical work still in process.<br /> <br /> In order to evolve themselves further, they tested the blood (and other parts) of supernatural creatures to note the effects.<br /> <br /> This new alchemy of the blood is said to be recently taking effects, whenether by mere logical conclusion of centuries of efforts or the awakening of the twisted sister of Marconius, concoctions gives effects of cainites.<br /> <br /> Currently in book, three types of effects are given<br /> <br /> -a merit which says that, as the result of ingesting large ammount of methuselah/faery/garou blood, the character can, with a willpower roll, manifest for the night a free point of chimery, animalism or auspex (not sure of the exact disciplines)<br /> <br /> -the dreadful mara disadvantage, which says that the player character consummed a thing that is still alive within him \u00e0 la failed diablery, tormenting him.<br /> <br /> Finally, a note at the end of the kyasid chapter gives a few exemple of potions with advantages and disadvantages<br /> <br /> Decoctions of garous would give points of strenght and proteism, but a higher sugestibility to frenzy.<br /> <br /> Potions mades from mages would give astral travel abilities and easier blood magic casting at the cost of weird coincidences if the cainite use masquerade breaking disciplines (aka paradox)<br /> <br /> And with delicious faeries, the vampire would potentially be able to temporarily walk in the sunlight, but be victil of &quot;hallucinatory&quot; creatures.<br /> <br /> In short, the vampire sort of superpose the states of the creatures onto himself.<br /> <br /> So, where would you lead that? 5 stepped paths based on creatures? An actually well made &quot;thin blood&quot; alchemy? A crafting list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T10:22:46-07:00","id":1457986,"title":"","content":"This seems to be mainly focused on consuming the elixirs, so there is no reason to make 'em just crafted concoctions with whatever difficulty and recipe availability you want for your chronicle. For a crossover or crossover-like chronicle this is an interesting option since it makes necessary adjustments available without much of a problem.<br /> <br /> If you want to delve deeper in it, though, someone already proposed around here the creation of a Path based on alchemy. As Paths goes that would be a more fitting option, although you could also envision a character that uses this alchemy as a means for other Paths, like Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> Aside that, a unique Discipline could be developed out from the consumption of such concoctions, either as a result of mutation/resonance or of the vampire making their own body into an Athanor, an alchemical furnace. This Disciplines could either work by passively solidifying on the character the benefits and disadvantages of the different creatures, or by being activated with Vitae take from specific creatures.<br /> <br /> On a side note, asking for V5 to be left out in the way you did is bad form to say the least. If your interest is in V20 (as is mine) just say so, but V5 is a thing and a part of this forum, deal with it. It is not about liking the game, it is about respecting and being mature with other players and their opinions and tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T07:27:32-07:00","id":1458053,"title":"","content":"How DnD do you want your alchemy?<br /> <br /> My understanding of things from looking up the real world inspiration: Actual alchemy is something thaumaturges (Vampire and mortal) use to improve themselves. Transforming yourself from lead to gold. Want thaumaturgy 1? Calculate and tailor to yourself a regime of chemical infusions, weird exercises, poisons... Purify yourself; higher level magic needs you to be ever more gold and ever less lead. Alongside deals with spirits and taking advantage of planetary allignments, alchemy is one of the three pillars of magic, according to hermeticism.<br /> <br /> A potion making power is just... lacking in profundities.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think Vamps should benefit from weird drinks. Vampirism itself is Alchemy in a few ways, and they are taking blood and turning into Vitae. Mixology is unnecessary (and limits such activities to the pretentious) . Just drinking the blood should be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T08:39:36-07:00","id":1458056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457978-kyasid-alchemy?p=1458053#post1458053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How DnD do you want your alchemy?<br /> <br /> My understanding of things from looking up the real world inspiration: Actual alchemy is something thaumaturges (Vampire and mortal) use to improve themselves. Transforming yourself from lead to gold. Want thaumaturgy 1? Calculate and tailor to yourself a regime of chemical infusions, weird exercises, poisons... Purify yourself; higher level magic needs you to be ever more gold and ever less lead. Alongside deals with spirits and taking advantage of planetary allignments, alchemy is one of the three pillars of magic, according to hermeticism.<br /> <br /> A potion making power is just... lacking in profundities.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think Vamps should benefit from weird drinks. Vampirism itself is Alchemy in a few ways, and they are taking blood and turning into Vitae. Mixology is unnecessary (and limits such activities to the pretentious) . Just drinking the blood should be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be fair, resuming alchemy as medieval self improvement is also lacking in historicity, it's both a spiritual practice and a litteral attempt at transforming matter.<br /> <br /> As for what kyasid alchemy look like in the book, it's about evolving the cainite position, so both the transformation of the self and the crafting part are here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}